{#
  NPC cross-player memories.
  Inject into NPC interaction/generation prompts.

  Makes NPCs remember encounters with OTHER players — the blacksmith
  recalls "a stranger asked about that sword last week" even though
  it was a different player's session.
#}

{% if currentNpc and currentNpc.name %}
{% set memories = getNpcMemories(currentNpc.name) %}
{% if memories and memories.length > 0 %}
<crossPlayerMemories>
{{ currentNpc.name }} has had interactions with other adventurers that they remember:
{% for mem in memories %}
  <memory>{{ mem.summary }}</memory>
{% endfor %}
Note: {{ currentNpc.name }} may reference these memories naturally in conversation, as things they experienced. They don't know these were "other players" — just other people they met.
</crossPlayerMemories>
{% endif %}

{# Déjà vu — echoes from other timelines #}
{% set deja = getDejaVu(currentNpc.name) %}
{% if deja %}
<dejaVu>
{{ currentNpc.name }} has a nagging sense of familiarity. Something about this conversation echoes a past encounter: "{{ deja }}". They may express this as an odd feeling of recognition, a half-remembered dream, or a sense that they've had this conversation before. Use subtly and only if it fits the moment.
</dejaVu>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
